WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.980
In the 1600s, a man planted a willow stem in a pot of dried soil.

2
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.400
The stem weighed 5 pounds.

3
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.300
The soil weighed 200 pounds.

4
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:19.860
Five years later, he reported a tree of about 169 pounds.

5
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.520
The soil was only about 2 ounces lighter.

6
00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.640
So where does a plant's mass come from?

7
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.700
And how does sunlight end up stored in sugar?

8
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.400
The answer starts with photosynthesis.

9
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:40.600
Plants, algae and cyanobacteria use light energy to turn carbon dioxide and water

10
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.300
into sugar. They release oxygen.

11
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.580
The sugar is glucose, a small sugar molecule with six carbon atoms.

12
00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:56.000
With formulas: six carbon dioxide plus six water plus light energy makes one glucose

13
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.840
plus six oxygen molecules.

14
00:00:58.733 --> 00:01:06.273
Count the atoms. On the left, there are 6 carbon, 12 hydrogen and 18 oxygen atoms.

15
00:01:06.973 --> 00:01:09.213
On the right, there are exactly the same.

16
00:01:10.013 --> 00:01:12.033
This is conservation of matter.

17
00:01:12.913 --> 00:01:17.833
In a chemical change, atoms are rearranged, never created or destroyed.

18
00:01:18.683 --> 00:01:21.003
Now the willow makes sense.

19
00:01:21.823 --> 00:01:27.343
The carbon and much of the oxygen in its sugar came from carbon dioxide in the air.

20
00:01:28.343 --> 00:01:29.923
The hydrogen came from water.

21
00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:35.643
The soil gave water and a small amount of minerals, so the dried soil barely

22
00:01:35.643 --> 00:01:42.343
changed. Most of a plant's dry mass, the mass left after drying, is built from

23
00:01:42.343 --> 00:01:44.543
carbon taken in as carbon dioxide.

24
00:01:45.483 --> 00:01:52.243
In plants and algae, photosynthesis happens in the chloroplast, a green organelle in

25
00:01:52.243 --> 00:01:57.123
leaf cells. Inside it, stacks of membranes hold chlorophyll.

26
00:01:58.043 --> 00:02:02.783
Chlorophyll is a green pigment that absorbs light, mostly red and blue.

27
00:02:03.743 --> 00:02:08.843
That captured energy powers the reactions that split water and build glucose.

28
00:02:09.843 --> 00:02:12.523
The oxygen released comes from the split water.

29
00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:15.563
Energy is conserved too.

30
00:02:16.463 --> 00:02:19.063
Light energy is not used up or made.

31
00:02:19.543 --> 00:02:25.423
It is transformed into chemical energy, energy held in the arrangement of atoms in

32
00:02:25.423 --> 00:02:31.683
molecules. Glucose and oxygen together hold more chemical energy than the carbon

33
00:02:31.683 --> 00:02:33.663
dioxide and water they came from.

34
00:02:34.523 --> 00:02:40.843
So a plant's dry mass comes mostly from carbon dioxide in the air, and sunlight is

35
00:02:40.843 --> 00:02:43.123
stored as chemical energy in sugar.
